## SQ-WCT-01 | six watering can ids, recipes
@group A
@commands Boot; grep latest.log for `hearthandharvest`, `watering_can`, `Error occurred while handling event`, `duplicate`
@pass six can ids registered once; recipes `creativedelight:...watering_can` and the five `smithing/..._watering_can` loaded; no error
@fails stale patcherMod still registering the id; NCH key missing in item_dict
@from batches/r1101/p1_server.qb
bootreject (?i)duplicate.*watering_can
> zq item hearthandharvest:watering_can
> zq item hearthandharvest:iron_watering_can
> zq item hearthandharvest:golden_watering_can
> zq item hearthandharvest:diamond_watering_can
> zq item hearthandharvest:netherite_watering_can
> zq item hearthandharvest:dragon_watering_can
> zq makes watering_can
reject Unknown item
expect creativedelight:.*watering_can -> 1 hearthandharvest:watering_can
count smithing/[a-z_]*watering_can >= 5
look six ids resolve once; base can recipe under creativedelight; five smithing recipes

## SQ-WCT-02 | cauldron fills by tier
@group A
@commands `/fill ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ minecraft:water_cauldron[level=3]`; bot holds `hearthandharvest:watering_can`, uses it on the cauldron; `data get entity <bot> SelectedItem`; `/execute if block ~ ~ ~ minecraft:water_cauldron[level=2]`. Repeat with `diamond_watering_can` (level 3 -> 1), `netherite_watering_can` (-> `minecraft:cauldron`), and an empty `diamond_watering_can` on `level=1`, an empty `netherite_watering_can` on `level=2`
@pass WaterLevel 8, cauldron level 2; diamond WaterLevel 20, level 1; netherite WaterLevel 32, empty cauldron; diamond on level 1: WaterLevel 10, empty cauldron; netherite on level 2: WaterLevel 21, empty cauldron
@fails cauldron interaction map claimed the click; level or partial-fill math
@from batches/r1101/p1_server.qb passed
> setblock -30 -60 -15 minecraft:water_cauldron[level=3]
> tp qa -30 -60 -13
> item replace entity qa weapon.mainhand with hearthandharvest:watering_can
> pbot use qa -30 -60 -15 up
> data get entity qa SelectedItem
> execute if block -30 -60 -15 minecraft:water_cauldron[level=2]
expect WaterLevel: 8
> setblock -30 -60 -15 minecraft:water_cauldron[level=3]
> item replace entity qa weapon.mainhand with hearthandharvest:diamond_watering_can
> pbot use qa -30 -60 -15 up
> data get entity qa SelectedItem
> execute if block -30 -60 -15 minecraft:water_cauldron[level=1]
expect WaterLevel: 20
> setblock -30 -60 -15 minecraft:water_cauldron[level=3]
> item replace entity qa weapon.mainhand with hearthandharvest:netherite_watering_can
> pbot use qa -30 -60 -15 up
> data get entity qa SelectedItem
> execute if block -30 -60 -15 minecraft:cauldron
expect WaterLevel: 32
> setblock -30 -60 -15 minecraft:water_cauldron[level=1]
> item replace entity qa weapon.mainhand with hearthandharvest:diamond_watering_can
> pbot use qa -30 -60 -15 up
> data get entity qa SelectedItem
expect WaterLevel: 10
> setblock -30 -60 -15 minecraft:water_cauldron[level=2]
> item replace entity qa weapon.mainhand with hearthandharvest:netherite_watering_can
> pbot use qa -30 -60 -15 up
> data get entity qa SelectedItem
expect WaterLevel: 21
count Test passed >= 3

## SQ-WCT-03 | Just a Well fills an iron can (lower and roof half)
@group A
@commands Place a Just a Well (`well:well`), wait for it to fill (or `/data merge block` its tank); bot uses `iron_watering_can` on the lower half, then on the roof half with an emptied can; `data get block <well>`
@pass WaterLevel 12 each time; tank down 1000 mB per fill
@fails well did not pass the click (fluid item check); roof half not routed below
@from batches/r1101/p1_server.qb
> setblock -36 -60 -15 well:well
> data get block -36 -60 -15
> data get block -36 -59 -15
sleep 20
> data get block -36 -60 -15
> tp qa -36 -60 -13
> item replace entity qa weapon.mainhand with hearthandharvest:iron_watering_can
> pbot use qa -36 -60 -15 north
> data get entity qa SelectedItem
> data get block -36 -60 -15
> item replace entity qa weapon.mainhand with hearthandharvest:iron_watering_can
> pbot use qa -36 -59 -15 north
> data get entity qa SelectedItem
> data get block -36 -60 -15
look WaterLevel 12 after each use; well tank down 1000 mB per fill; an empty well (no rain / no water below) = setup, not the can: record the tank NBT

## SQ-WCT-04 | dragon can soaks 7x7, copper can the centre only
@group A
@commands `/fill ~-3 ~-1 ~-3 ~3 ~-1 ~3 minecraft:farmland[moisture=0]`, `/fill ~-3 ~ ~-3 ~3 ~ ~3 minecraft:wheat[age=7]`; bot with `dragon_watering_can{WaterLevel:64}` uses it on the centre; `/execute if block ~3 ~-1 ~3 minecraft:farmland[moisture=7]` and the corner `~-3 ~-1 ~-3`; repeat on fresh soil with `watering_can{WaterLevel:8}`, check `~1 ~-1 ~` stays dry
@pass 7x7 soaked, WaterLevel 63; copper soaks the centre only
@fails area spans
@from batches/r1101/p1_server.qb passed
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 0
> fill -43 -61 -33 -37 -61 -27 minecraft:farmland[moisture=0]
> fill -43 -60 -33 -37 -60 -27 minecraft:wheat[age=0]
> item replace entity qa weapon.mainhand with hearthandharvest:dragon_watering_can{WaterLevel:64}
> item replace entity qa weapon.offhand with minecraft:air
> tp qa -40 -60 -35
> pbot use qa -40 -60 -30 up
> data get entity qa SelectedItem
> execute if block -37 -61 -27 minecraft:farmland[moisture=7]
> execute if block -43 -61 -33 minecraft:farmland[moisture=7]
expect WaterLevel: 63
count Test passed >= 2
> fill -43 -61 -33 -37 -61 -27 minecraft:farmland[moisture=0]
> item replace entity qa weapon.mainhand with hearthandharvest:watering_can{WaterLevel:8}
> pbot use qa -40 -60 -30 up
