## SQ-WCT-05 | diamond can smithing recipe; over-full can clamps
@group A
@commands Bot has `golden_watering_can{WaterLevel:5,BonemealLevel:3,FertilizerItem:"minecraft:bone_meal"}`, a diamond in the inventory; smithing is a GUI, so check the recipe instead: grep the recipe dump for `smithing/diamond_watering_can`; give `watering_can{WaterLevel:16,BonemealLevel:16}` and `data get` after a soil use
@pass recipe base golden can, addition diamond; old can reads 8, drops to 7 after the use
@fails recipe id; clamp on read
@from batches/r1101/p1_server.qb
> zq rdetail smithing/diamond_watering_can
expect golden_watering_can
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 0
> setblock -48 -61 -30 minecraft:farmland[moisture=0]
> setblock -48 -60 -30 minecraft:wheat[age=0]
> item replace entity qa weapon.mainhand with hearthandharvest:watering_can{WaterLevel:16,BonemealLevel:16}
> tp qa -48 -60 -32
> pbot use qa -48 -60 -30 up
> data get entity qa SelectedItem
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
look smithing base golden can, addition diamond; old can reads 8 and drops to 7 after the use (WaterLevel 7 in the NBT, or 15 if the clamp is on read only: record)
